<div class="diagram-notes">
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px"><span style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent)">1 · All realtime state in one pod</span><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.5; color: #2E2B26">The chat hub, matchmaking sockets, admin feed and rate limiter are Go maps in memory. A second replica would split users across pods. Redis pub/sub is the fan-out when it's time to scale.</p></div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px"><span style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent)">2 · Redis is on the sign-in path</span><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.5; color: #2E2B26">OTP codes, OTP rate limits, the JWT denylist and slot holds all sit in one Redis pod. If it restarts, sign-in and slot holds stop until it's back.</p></div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px"><span style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent)">3 · Migrations are a manual step</span><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.5; color: #2E2B26">Jenkins compiles cmd/migrate but never runs it. A rollout that needs a schema change needs make migrate-up against RDS first.</p></div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px"><span style="font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent)">4 · Config still has placeholders</span><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.5; color: #2E2B26">ALLOWED_ORIGINS and COOKIE_DOMAIN hold example domains, so the browser-based admin panel fails CORS until they're real. The mobile app isn't affected.</p></div>
</div>
